// Clark County, Ohio — curated directory of meaningful links.
// Single source of truth for the app. Keep entries verified and current.
// Fields: name, category, subcategory, url, description
// Last reviewed: 2026-11-09
//
// Every URL below was fetched and its content checked against the organization
// it claims to be. Sites that block automated fetching (JFS and the New Carlisle
// library) were checked in a browser.
//
// THINGS THAT CHANGED SINCE JULY
//
//   * clarkdjfs.org now redirects to clarkcountyohiodjfs.gov; newcarlisle.net to
//     newcarlisleohio.gov; moorefieldtownship.com to moorefieldtownshipclark.gov.
//   * expandgreaterspringfield.com no longer loads; the CIC's live presence is
//     clarkcounty.jobs (administered by the Greater Springfield Partnership).
//   * SCAT bus service has been replaced by "Field Trips", an on-demand service.
//   * The health district now calls itself the Clark County Health Department
//     (clarkhealthohio.gov redirects to ccchd.com).
//   * www.clarkcountyauditor.org serves a stale 2019 page; the non-www address is
//     current. WellSpring (Springfield) has closed; springfieldchristian.com is a
//     domain for sale. The Springfield YMCA is now part of the YMCA of Greater
//     Dayton.
//
// TRAPS
//
//   Clark County NEVADA (Las Vegas) and WASHINGTON (Vancouver) dominate searches.
//   The county's own directory gives betheltownship.org for Bethel Township, but
//   that site is MIAMI County's Bethel Township. pleasanttownship.org is another
//   county's; tremontil.gov is Illinois. Young's Jersey Dairy, John Bryan State
//   Park, Glen Helen and Clifton are Greene County.
//
// GEOGRAPHY
//
//   * Two cities (Springfield, New Carlisle); villages Enon and South Vienna have
//     sites, Catawba, Donnelsville, North Hampton, South Charleston and Tremont
//     City do not. Five of ten townships have sites.
//   * Three Greene County districts (Cedar Cliff, Fairborn, Yellow Springs) take
//     in parts of Clark townships; they are flagged.
//   * The mental-health board serves Clark, Greene and Madison; United Way and
//     Second Harvest serve Clark, Champaign and Madison/Logan; Head Start is run by
//     Miami Valley Child Development Centers (Dayton); Habitat is the Greater
//     Dayton affiliate.
//   * WYSO and WEEC are flagged: WYSO is in Yellow Springs; WEEC's studios are in
//     Xenia.
//
// LEFT OUT rather than listed unverified: the Probate and Juvenile court sites
// (do not load), the Clark County ESC (its only site needs a sign-in), the
// Auditor's GIS and Treasurer payment sites (errors), the Port Authority (no
// site), the substance-abuse coalition (dead domain), the SPCA and Animal Welfare
// League (no first-party sites) and Sheltered Inc. (status unclear).

